    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focusing exclusively on \"equality of outcome\" in credit scoring is generally not considered the most ethically sound approach, as it can lead to lists that are less predictive of actual creditworthiness and fail to account for individual circumstances. Ethical AI frameworks typically prioritize \"equality of opportunity\" (fairness in treatment) or calibrated fairness, which ensure that different groups are judged by the same standards without compromising the model's overall accuracy. For a fintech startup, adopting a balanced approach that meets business goals while minimizing harmful biases often yields more sustainable and legally defensible results.",
